        "original_id": "3a3b02b4-49ca-5779-a3b0-11dd218df67a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norman L. Buckley, Peter Paige, Bradley Bredeweg, I. Marlene King, Tyler Blackburn\n- TV Series: The O.C., Chuck, Gossip Girl, Pretty Little Liars, The Fosters, Ravenswood, Miss Me × 100\n- Organizations: Freeform, ABC Family\n- Roles: television director, editor, showrunner\n\nFacts:\n- Norman L. Buckley was born on November 25, 1955.\n- Norman L. Buckley is an American television director and editor.\n- Norman L. Buckley is best known for his work on The O.C., Chuck, Gossip Girl, Pretty Little Liars, and The Fosters.\n- The Fosters is an American family drama television series created by Peter Paige and Bradley Bredeweg.\n- The Fosters premiered in the United States on June 3, 2013 on the television network Freeform, which was previously named ABC Family.\n- Miss Me × 100 was directed by Norman Buckley.\n- Miss Me × 100 was written by showrunner I. Marlene King.\n- Miss Me × 100 features the return of Tyler Blackburn as Caleb Rivers after his departure from Pretty Little Liars in its fourth season for the sister show Ravenswood.",
